`tempSvg` is appended to `document.body` for bounding-box measurement but is only removed on the happy path. If `configureLabelImages` (line 68) throws, `tempSvg.remove()` at line 81 is never reached, leaking a hidden SVG element into the live DOM. Per project rules, measurement elements must always be removed. Wrap the block in a `try/finally`:
```js
try {
  await configureLabelImages(div.node(), node.label);
  // ... bbox logic ...
} finally {
  tempSvg.remove();
}
```
The same issue exists in `packages/mermaid/src/dagre-wrapper/createLabel.js` at line 59.

`getConfig()` is called twice inside `setupImage()` (lines 34 and 35) every time an image fires its load/error event. Per project rules, `getConfig()` should be called once per rendering entry point and cached. Move the call to the top of `configureLabelImages` (before the `Promise.all`) and pass the result into `setupImage` via closure:
```ts
const config = getConfig();
const bodyFontSize = config.fontSize ?? window.getComputedStyle(document.body).fontSize;
```
